# Zentro App Development Rules

## 🪙 Currency Standards

- **Primary Currency**: UGX (Ugandan Shillings)
- **Display Format**: No decimal places needed (e.g., "UGX 1500" not "UGX 15.00")
- **Price Fields**: Use `unit_price` with integer values
- **Formatting**: Use `.toFixed(0)` for price displays, `.toLocaleString()` for large numbers

## 🔌 API Endpoints

Based on the Django backend structure at `zentro-backend`, use these correct endpoints:

### Items Management

- `GET /api/items/` - List all items
- `POST /api/items/` - Create new item
- `GET /api/items/{id}/` - Get specific item
- `PUT /api/items/{id}/` - Update item
- `DELETE /api/items/{id}/` - Delete item

### Categories

- `GET /api/categories/` - List item categories (NOT `/api/items/item-categories/`)

### Item Journals

- `GET /api/item-journals/` - List item journal entries (NOT `/api/items/item-journal/`)
- `PUT /api/item-journals/{id}/` - Update item journal (NOT `/api/items/item-journal/{id}/`)

### Sales

- `GET /api/sales/` - List sales
- `POST /api/sales/` - Create sale
- `GET /api/sales/generate-invoice-no/` - Generate invoice number

### Authentication

- `POST /api/auth/token/` - Login & get JWT
- `POST /api/auth/verify-otp/` - Verify OTP
- `GET /api/auth/profile/` - Get user profile

## 🏗️ Multi-Tenant Architecture

- **Base URL Pattern**: `https://{tenant}.zentroapp-backend.com`
- **Fallback URL**: `https://zentroapp-backend.com`
- **Tenant Storage**: Use AsyncStorage key 'tenant'
- **Axios Instance**: Create tenant-specific instances using `createAxiosInstance(tenant)`

## 📱 React Native Conventions

- **Component Naming**: Use PascalCase (e.g., `Items.tsx`, `EditItemModal`)
- **State Variables**: Use camelCase (e.g., `selectedItem`, `items`)
- **Function Names**: Use camelCase (e.g., `handleEditItem`, `loadItems`)
- **Interface Names**: Use PascalCase (e.g., `Item`, `PaginatedResponse`)
- **Loading States**: Use descriptive names (e.g., `loading`, `searchLoading`, `categoriesLoading`)

## 🛡️ Error Handling

- **API Responses**: Always check `response && response.results && Array.isArray(response.results)`
- **Null Safety**: Use optional chaining (`item?.id?.toString()`) and fallbacks
- **State Management**: Reset arrays to `[]` and counts to `0` on errors
- **User Feedback**: Show meaningful error messages, not technical details

## 🔒 Security

- **JWT Tokens**: Store in AsyncStorage, include in Authorization header
- **API Keys**: Never hardcode, use environment variables
- **Input Validation**: Validate all user inputs before API calls
- **Error Logging**: Log errors for debugging but don't expose sensitive data

## 📊 Data Models

- **Item Structure**: `{ id, item_name, unit_price, inventory, item_images, ... }`
- **Pagination**: Use `page` parameter with `itemsPerPage` limit
- **Search**: Use `q` parameter for search queries
- **Images**: Handle `item_images` array with fallback to placeholder

## 🎨 UI/UX Standards

- **Loading States**: Show loading indicators during API calls
  - Main content loading: Large spinner with descriptive text ("Loading items...")
  - Search loading: Small spinner in search bar during search operations
  - Form loading: Spinners in specific form sections (e.g., category picker)
  - Use `ActivityIndicator` with appropriate sizes and colors
- **Empty States**: Display helpful messages when no data exists
- **Refresh Control**: Implement pull-to-refresh for lists
- **Form Validation**: Validate forms before submission
- **Success Feedback**: Show confirmation messages after successful operations

## 🧪 Testing

- **Unit Tests**: Test individual components and functions
- **Integration Tests**: Test API interactions
- **Error Scenarios**: Test error handling and edge cases
- **Performance**: Monitor API response times and app performance

## 📝 Documentation

- **Code Comments**: Explain complex logic and business rules
- **API Documentation**: Keep endpoint documentation updated
- **Change Log**: Document breaking changes and new features
- **README**: Maintain project setup and usage instructions

## 🚀 Performance

- **Image Optimization**: Use appropriate image sizes and formats
- **API Caching**: Implement caching for frequently accessed data
- **Lazy Loading**: Load data only when needed
- **Bundle Size**: Keep dependencies minimal and optimized

## 🔄 Version Control

- **Commit Messages**: Use descriptive, conventional commit format
- **Branch Naming**: Use feature/ prefix for new features
- **Code Review**: Require review before merging to main
- **Hotfixes**: Use hotfix/ prefix for urgent fixes
